    "text": "Remote Logging > Remote Login is a process in which user can login into remote computer and use services that are available on the remote computer. It is implemented using Telnet. Example: Students may want to connect to their university computer lab from their home to access application programs for doing homework assignments. > One way is to create a client/server application program for each desired service using FTP or SMTP but it would be impossible to write a specific client/server program for each demand. > Better solution is remote login that lets a user access any application program on a remote computer. After logging on, a user can use the services available on the remote computer and transfer the results back to the local computer.",
